qylock lock-screen fixes for this rice (applied by lockscreen/apply-patches.sh).
Derived from qylock by Darkkal44 (https://github.com/Darkkal44/qylock),
licensed GPL-3.0; this patch is under GPL-3.0 too (not this repo's MIT license).
Base: qylock c2933f27b655a999911e6699e1b2c67e59cbd428.

quickshell-lockscreen/shim/SddmShim.qml (the lock screen's login code):
- An empty password (Enter pressed to wake the screen) no longer starts PAM.
  Before, that PAM conversation waited forever for an answer and every later
  attempt was silently ignored ("already running"): no error, and even the
  right password didn't unlock (2026-11-13).
- A new attempt while PAM still waits answers it or restarts PAM.
- PAM errors and a 20 s timeout end an attempt with an error instead of hanging.
- PAM's own message (e.g. faillock: "The account is locked due to 3 failed
  logins ...") is passed to the theme as sddm.lastError.
themes/winter/Main.qml:
- Shows sddm.lastError when there is one (else "ACCESS DENIED"); the error
  line wraps. SDDM's own login screen has no lastError, so it's unchanged.

